\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+5)-1\n$$\n\nNote that in the equation above, we have $y={g}^{-1}(x).$\n\n**Step 2:** Next, we differentiate. The overall goal is to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ but the equation is already solved for $x,$ so we compute $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y}$ and then take the reciprocal:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y+5)-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5)\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y+5)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2y+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Lastly, we write the result in terms of ${g}^{-1}(x).$ Since $y={g}^{-1}(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[{g}^{-1}(x)] & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5) \\\\ {({g}^{-1})}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279453 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279454 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279455 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279456 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1000 #edb/ref 17592186279457 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1041 "selection" 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1104 #edb/ref 17592186279453 13194139534159 true] [17592186279452 1110 #uuid "60906cdb-5041-50be-ae27-7859b2067606" 13194139534159 true] [17592186279453 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2{g}^{-1}(x)+5)" 13194139534159 true] [17592186279453 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534159 true] [17592186279453 1111 #uuid "3410f762-ea3c-5fae-90f5-092500ff7908" 13194139534159 true] [17592186279454 1034 "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡(2{g}^{-1}